  "notes": "USAGE:\nA literary and somewhat formal word. Used for abstract concepts like life, peace, tradition, freedom, and human rights. Common in speeches, essays, and formal writing.\n\nALTERNATIVE READING:\nThe same kanji {尊|たっと}ぶ can also be read たっとぶ with the same meaning. Both readings are standard.\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {大切|たいせつ}にする: to treat with care (more everyday)\n- {重|おも}んじる: to attach importance to (formal)\n- {敬|うやま}う: to respect, to revere (focuses more on people)\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {命|いのち}を{尊|とうと}ぶ: to value life\n- {平和|へいわ}を{尊|とうと}ぶ: to value peace\n- {自由|じゆう}を{尊|とうと}ぶ: to value freedom\n- {伝統|でんとう}を{尊|とうと}ぶ: to value tradition\n- {人権|じんけん}を{尊|とうと}ぶ: to value human rights",
